  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.639) shows that multimodal fusion with weighted combination and avgpool aggregation is the strongest configuration. However, the image modality is very weak in isolation (config_010: resnet50 singleprofile, acc=0.208), raising the question of whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) could contribute more informative features to the fusion. This experiment (config_025) is a clean single-variable extension of config_019, changing only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping all validated settings (multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion, pca_n2000). It directly tests whether the image branch is a bottleneck and whether upgrading it yields meaningful multimodal gains. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information experiment: it either confirms that the current resnet50 features are sufficient (allowing us to focus on RNA encoder improvements) or reveals that a stronger visual backbone unlocks substantially better multimodal performance, guiding all subsequent experiments."
}

